WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:07.419
After dinner Ray got ready to go out.

2
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.247
"The computer at the diner is getting old," he said.

3
00:00:10.248 --> 00:00:12.691
"I'm going to the store to look into buying a new one.

4
00:00:12.692 --> 00:00:16.959
I'll be back in a little while."

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.079
When he was gone, Mateo and Ally went into her room.

6
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:28.009
"Wow, that was really big news from Papi about Big City Foods," Mateo said.

7
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:34.985
"And speaking of big news, you have to finish telling me how you know that Melanie's not the Jorgandian."

8
00:00:34.986 --> 00:00:38.839
But before Ally could say anything, Alpha's screen blinked on.

9
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.219
"I could have told you that the life-form from the diner is not Jorgandian.

10
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:51.367
While my sensors and memory bank are impaired by this inferior technology, I am capable of detecting human life-forms."

11
00:00:51.368 --> 00:00:57.018
"What?" Ally cried. "Why didn't you tell us that before?"

12
00:00:57.019 --> 00:01:00.209
"You didn't ask," Alpha said.

13
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.259
Mateo shook his head.

14
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:09.228
"So, you can't figure out who the Jorgandian is, but you can figure out who it isn't?"

15
00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:13.620
"Affirmative. I have scanned everyone who works at Ray's Diner.

16
00:01:13.621 --> 00:01:19.069
All the employees are humans, as are your friends Kate and Bethany."

17
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:27.767
"Phew!" Ally said. "That's a huge relief!"

18
00:01:27.768 --> 00:01:32.879
The next morning Ally was eating breakfast in the dining room when Mateo walked in.

19
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:39.115
"Hey, Ally," he said. "I can walk to work with you today, but we have to leave really soon.

20
00:01:39.116 --> 00:01:46.128
I got a text from Coach Cross. He asked me to meet him at the soccer field before camp starts."

21
00:01:46.129 --> 00:01:48.261
"It's okay," Ally said.

22
00:01:48.262 --> 00:01:54.021
"I can walk to work on my own." She looked at Mateo.

23
00:01:54.022 --> 00:01:57.024
"Are you sad that camp is almost over?"

24
00:01:57.025 --> 00:02:02.946
"Yes, but I'm also excited for school to start soon," Mateo said.

25
00:02:02.947 --> 00:02:06.259
"Oh right, school," Ally mumbled.

26
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:13.036
"I can't believe it," she thought, "but I actually miss going to school sometimes.

27
00:02:13.037 --> 00:02:18.760
I wonder what my classmates on Astralia will be studying this year."

28
00:02:18.761 --> 00:02:22.879
"Are you alright?" Mateo asked.

29
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.830
"Yep, I'm fine," Ally said.

30
00:02:25.831 --> 00:02:32.534
"Go meet Coach Cross. I can read minds on my way into town, to see if I can find the Jorgandian.

31
00:02:32.535 --> 00:02:38.095
Besides, I have to stop at the copy shop to pick up the menus."

32
00:02:38.096 --> 00:02:43.383
"Okay," Mateo said. "Text me if you need me."

33
00:02:43.384 --> 00:02:48.675
When Ally arrived at the copy shop, the door was locked.

34
00:02:48.676 --> 00:02:54.104
"Eli's not in yet," she thought. "I'll come back later."

35
00:02:54.105 --> 00:02:57.522
But suddenly he appeared at the door.

36
00:02:57.523 --> 00:03:03.319
"He looks even paler than he did yesterday," Ally thought as he unlocked the door.

37
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:09.309
"Come inside, quickly!" Eli pulled Ally into the shop.

38
00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.867
"Are you feeling alright, Eli?" Ally asked.

39
00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:16.807
"Maybe you should close the store and go home to rest."

40
00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:22.081
Eli grunted. "Stay here. Do not move."

41
00:03:22.082 --> 00:03:26.756
While Eli went into the back room, Ally lifted the window shades.

42
00:03:26.757 --> 00:03:31.033
As people walked by, she read their minds.

43
00:03:31.034 --> 00:03:34.853
"They're all humans," Ally thought with relief.

44
00:03:34.854 --> 00:03:37.399
"No Jorgandians out there!"

45
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:43.933
"What are you doing?" Eli was back behind the counter, holding a bag with the printed menus.

46
00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:47.299
"Close the shades. You and I have business to finish."

47
00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:53.364
"Sorry about that." Ally started to close the shades when she spotted Kate and Bethany out on the street.

48
00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:59.762
"Oh! My friends. I haven't seen them since I got back to town!"

49
00:03:59.763 --> 00:04:03.139
Ally grabbed the bag of menus and ran toward the door.

50
00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.979
"I'll just take these with me. Thanks!"

51
00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.170
Eli shouted something at her.

52
00:04:08.171 --> 00:04:12.274
"Just put the copies on Ray's bill, please!"

53
00:04:12.275 --> 00:04:17.092
Ally ran to catch up with her friends. "Wait for me, girls!"

54
00:04:17.093 --> 00:04:23.059
"Hi, Ally!" Kate said. "It's so nice to see you!"

55
00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:28.650
"We're on our way to the diner for breakfast." Bethany smiled.

56
00:04:28.651 --> 00:04:37.690
"Now we can all walk there together!"

57
00:04:37.691 --> 00:04:41.399
At Ray's, Tina was placing a takeout order with Flo.

58
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.940
"I'd like an extra doughnut, please," Tina said.

59
00:04:44.941 --> 00:04:47.039
"It's for Dr. Lloyd.

60
00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:53.047
He's invited me to visit his lab tomorrow, so I want to bring him a treat today."

61
00:04:53.048 --> 00:04:56.640
"That's nice," Flo said.

62
00:04:56.641 --> 00:05:01.759
Tina got her order and headed for the door. But before leaving, she turned to Ally.

63
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:07.672
"Remember, be safe out there."

64
00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:11.253
Ally felt a chill travel down her spine.

65
00:05:11.254 --> 00:05:14.350
"What was that about, Ally?" Kate asked.

66
00:05:14.351 --> 00:05:20.119
Bethany laughed. "Tina is a security guard.

67
00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.270
She's probably always thinking about security!"

68
00:05:24.271 --> 00:05:28.001
Meanwhile Ally was thinking about something else.

69
00:05:28.002 --> 00:05:32.590
"Tina's new in town, and she has a keen interest in space.

70
00:05:32.591 --> 00:05:40.253
Plus, she's been trying to get close to Dr. Lloyd. Oh no!"

71
00:05:40.254 --> 00:05:45.499
Ally dropped onto a counter stool, horrified by what had just dawned on her.

72
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:50.160
"What if Tina is the Jorgandian?"

